From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:35:59 +0000\
Subject: [PATCH] Add procedurally generated random clouds to the sky\
\
Add a self-bootstrapping ProceduralClouds component that spawns a\
randomised cloudscape high in the skybox on every run of the gameplay\
scenes (CricketVR, Nets). Each run randomises cloud count, placement\
(azimuth/elevation on the sky dome), per-cloud shape (overlapping\
squashed ellipsoid puffs), scale and yaw, so the sky looks different\
each time the scene is played. Clouds drift slowly around the vertical\
axis. A URP-lit matte white material is built at runtime so the clouds\
catch the scene's directional light; an optional inspector seed allows\
reproducing a specific layout.\
\
The component auto-spawns via RuntimeInitializeOnLoadMethod, so no\
scene authoring or manual wiring is required.\
\
